25Disinfection of the overall plant                                       000338
26   Professional disinfection and subsequent flushing of                 000339
26   all plant parts in the scope of supply that are in                   000340
26   contact with drinking water, incl. pumps, surge                      000341
26   vessels, filter vessels and clean water tanks and other              000342
26   units and valves, for commissioning with proof of                    000343
26   freedom from germs by a certified laboratory.                        000344
26                                                                        000345
26   Required are at least 3 samples in succession with                   000346
26   negative biological findings (scope of examination                   000347
26   Pseudomonas aeruginosa, PER000160 bacteria, Escherichia              000348
26   coli, enterococci, culturable microorganisms as colony               000349
26   count at 22 øC and 36 øC).                                           000350
26                                                                        000351
26   The proof samples are to be taken at the raw water                   000352
26   inlet and at the clean water outlet of the waterworks                000353
26   (i.e. 3 samplings at 2 sampling points each).                        000354
26                                                                        000355
26   Execution in several stages according to the                         000356
26   requirements of the plant configuration.                             000357
26                                                                        000358
26   The billing of any further disinfections required is on              000359
26   the basis of actual time and material against proof,                 000360
26   but only as far as the contractor is not responsible                 000361
26   for the repeated disinfection.                                       000362
26                                                                        000363
26   Note on vessel disinfection (filters):                               000364
26   The disinfection of the filter bed of the arsenic                    000365
26   removal filters is dealt with in a separate item in the              000366
26   division "Equipment arsenication filters".                           000367
26   The AN alone is responsible for the harmless disposal                000368
26   of the waste water including any neutralisation                      000369
26   required.                                                            000370
26   It is to be taken into account that the property                     000371
26   drainage (wastewater) is by means of a lifting unit,                 000372
26   which is designed for a delivery rate of approx. 8                   000373
26   m3/h. The disposal of larger quantities of waste water               000374
26   is therefore possibly associated with a higher                       000375
26   expenditure of time, unless buffer tanks for the                     000376
26   intermediate storage of waste water are kept available               000377
26   on site.                                                             000378
26   For the period of the disinfection it is to be assumed               000379
26   for the cost estimate that no valves are yet                         000380
26   electrically connected, i.e. corresponding expenditure               000381
26   of time for manual on-site operation is to be included               000382
26   in the price and is not paid separately.                             000383
26                                                                        000384
26   Disinfectant e.g. [PERSON_000000000000000065] or                     000385
26   equivalent.                                                          000386
