20                                                                        001007
26   [PERSON_00000000000128] high-performance - cross-flow                001008
26   aeration system for physical deacidification                         001009
26                                                                        001010
26   For designs that deviate from the following                          001011
26   description, the equivalence is to be proven by                      001012
26   meaningful documents (design description, data sheets).              001013
26                                                                        001014
26   Cross-flow aeration system or [PERSON_00000066] for                  001015
26   physical deacidification of drinking water in                        001016
26   energetically optimised design.                                      001017
26   By fine-bubble air injection via ceramic elements of                 001018
26   glass-bonded sintered material the carbonic acid is                  001019
26   stripped out; Simple aerator cassette change by means                001020
26   of side pull-out and lateral opening elements.                       001021
26   Depending on item text in one or two-storey design;                  001022
26   Entire apparatus ([PERSON_00000066]) executed gas-tight              001023
26   in pressure stage 3/6 according to DIN 24190                         001024
26   (+6500/-500 Pa); Tightness class IV according to DIN EN              001025
26   1507 with highest requirement, limit value of the air                001026
26   leakage rate class acc. to D DIN E1507 < 0,006 cmü/min;              001027
26   The gas tightness is to be proven to the client on                   001028
26   request;                                                             001029
26   Complete apparatus described below fabricated as sheet               001030
26   metal construction, in predominantly folded and bolted               001031
26   execution, welding stresses are to be minimised,                     001032
26   therefore all casing stiffeners are to be connected                  001033
26   force-fit to the sheet metal construction without                    001034
26   welding; Minimum material thickness for the entire                   001035
26   construction 3 mm; All steel parts in stainless PER89                001036
26   with the material no. 1.4571, fabricated in                          001037
26   ferrite-free rooms and after processing pickled and                  001038
26   passivated in a full bath; Packed in film at the                     001039
26   factory and assembled with film;                                     001040
26   All bolted connections (e.g. cover bolting) that cannot              001041
26   be executed as through bolting are to be produced with               001042
26   easily exchangeable thread inserts i.e. threaded holes               001043
26   in sheet metal parts are not permitted; The aeration                 001044
26   system is built up Modular; The modules connected in                 001045
26   series (train) are connected horizontally by means of                001046
26   rectangular flange; In order to guarantee a permanent                001047
26   tightness between the modules, a sealing system is used              001048
26   that is able to decouple the weight forces to be                     001049
26   transmitted from the sealing forces needed, i.e. a                   001050
26   force-fit connection is produced between the metals;                 001051
26   This sealing system (hereinafter called connection                   001052
26   adapter with sealing device) is clamped in each case                 001053
26   between the modules to be connected and consists of one              001054
26   solid rectangular flange each with corresponding                     001055
26   connection threads as well as O-ring seals worked in                 001056
26   all round with a hardness of 40 Shore; The aeration                  001057
26   elements must meet the requirements of the KTW and pass              001058
26   the tests for microbiological growth (DVGW worksheet                 001059
26   W270); Casing and cover seals by means of profile seal               001060
26   with KTW and DVGW W270 approval with a minimum Shore                 001061
26   hardness of 40ø, according to DIN53505 and DIN7868 (use              001062
26   of sealing compounds excluded); A detail design drawing              001063
26   of the complete [PERSON_00000066]s is to be included in              001064
26   the prices and submitted to site management in good                  001065
26   time before ordering for checking and approval; Because              001066
26   of the high energy efficiency required, all components               001067
