25Disinfection of arsenic removal filters                                 001929
26   After completion of the installation flushing, a                     001930
26   separate disinfection of the open arsenic removal                    001931
26   filters with hydrogen peroxide is to be carried out                  001932
26   according to manufacturer's recommendation GEH©.                     001933
26   The disinfectant, e.g. 1 container Veolia Hydrex 9561                001934
26   per filter, is to be introduced into the filter.                     001935
26   After an exposure time of at least 2 hours, a                        001936
26   disinfection flushing in upflow to remove the PER029                 001937
26   loaded with disinfectant from the adsorber bed,                      001938
26   backwash velocity 26 m/h, will to be carried out;                    001939
26   flushing until the outflow water is free of turbidity                001940
26   and for multiple water exchange in the filter bed,                   001941
26   duration at least 10 minutes.                                        001942
