26   General regulations for execution:                                   002093
26                                                                        002094
26   The requirements and designs listed below are to be                  002095
26   complied with and to be included in the price of the                 002096
26   respective pipeline items.                                           002097
26                                                                        002098
26   Connection points:                                                   002099
26   All connection points (position, dimension) are to be                002100
26   surveyed exactly on site. The details in the tender                  002101
26   documents do not release the bidder from this                        002102
26   obligation. Subsequent claims based on failure to carry              002103
26   out the survey are not recognised.                                   002104
26                                                                        002105
26   Venting/air admission and drains                                     002106
26   Unless otherwise required, venting/ air admission                    002107
26   facilities are to be provided at unavoidable high                    002108
26   points of liquid-carrying pipelines and drain                        002109
26   facilities at low points.                                            002110
26                                                                        002111
26   Pipe connections                                                     002112
26   All pipelines must be connected with easily detachable               002113
26   screw, clamp or compression connections or, for nominal              002114
26   diameters > DN 50, exclusively with flange connections               002115
26   to each other as well as to the tanks, wall                          002116
26   penetrations, valves, measuring devices etc. For                     002117
26   connections of different metallic materials (e.g.                    002118
26   filter tank - stainless steel line, but also components              002119
26   with non-conductive external corrosion protection, e.g.              002120
26   EKB) including supports, clamps etc., an electrical                  002121
26   separation "insulating flange" is to be provided to                  002122
26   prevent contact corrosion.                                           002123
26   Surcharges to the usual flange connections of the                    002124
26   nominal diameters to be offered in this LV for                       002125
26   producing an electrical separation point at flange                   002126
26   connection to avoid corrosion consisting of:                         002127
26   on piece insulating flange gasket,                                   002128
26   insulating sleeves, one piece per hole                               002129
26   insulating washers, two pieces per hole                              002130
26   steel washers, two pieces per hole                                   002131
26   are to be included in the unit prices of the valves to               002132
26   be installed.                                                        002133
26                                                                        002134
26   For electrical consumers installed in stainless steel                002135
26   pipelines (valves,measuring devices etc.), earthing                  002136
26   lugs for connection by others on site of an earthing                 002137
26   cable connection must in addition be welded onto the                 002138
26   adjoining stainless steel pipeline parts.                            002139
26                                                                        002140
26   Drinking-water-carrying pipelines from DN 65 and                     002141
26   larger, in flange-saving design, incl. all necessary                 002142
26   components (e.g. welding flanges etc.) welding                       002143
26   consumables and auxiliary materials, in particular                   002144
26   observing the following specification:                               002145
26   permissible component size max. fitting length 5.000 mm              002146
26   max. fitting width for outlets and bends 1.500 mm                    002147
26   Material: all pipes, bends, reducers and flanges in                  002148
26   material number 1.4571                                               002149
26   Pipes: longitudinally welded and pickled round pipes  v              002150
26   = 1,0, DIN EN 10216-5.                                               002151
26   The minimum wall thickness of the pipes is to be                     002152
26   designed according to the max. operating pressures                   002153
26   occurring acc. to AD-Merkblatt B0 and B1 and the                     002154
26   structural requirements, whereby the max. deflection of              002155
26   the pipeline in the ready-for-operation state is set at              002156
26   one four-hundredth of the span. A structural proof is                002157
26   to be provided on request of site management.                        002158
26   If the requirements from structural analysis or welded               002159
26   connections result in smaller wall thicknesses, at                   002160
26   least the following wall thicknesses are nevertheless                002161
26   to be complied with:                                                 002162
26   DN 10 - 32: 2,0 mm                                                   002163
26   DN 40 - 80: 2,0 mm                                                   002164
26   DN 100 - 150: 2,6 mm                                                 002165
26   DN 200: 2,9 mm                                                       002166
26   DN 250: 3,0 mm                                                       002167
26   DN 300 - 350: 3,2 mm                                                 002168
26   DN 400 - 500: 4,0 mm                                                 002169
26   DN 600 - 1000: 5,0 mm                                                002170
26                                                                        002171
26   Bends: longitudinally welded and pickled bends type 3;               002172
26   from DN 400 R = d + 100                                              002173
26   Reducers: longitudinally welded and pickled reducers;                002174
26   overall length according to DIN EN 10253; minimum wall               002175
26   thickness according to pipe wall thickness                           002176
26   Flanges: acc. to DIN EN 1092-1                                       002177
26                                                                        002178
26   Requirements for the manufacturing plant of the                      002179
26   pipelines:                                                           002180
26   All fittings are to be manufactured at the works ready               002181
26   for assembly in ferrite-free rooms. Manufacture in                   002182
26   rooms in which ferritic steels are also processed is                 002183
26   not permitted. In addition, only ferrite-free tools and              002184
26   lifting gear may be used for processing the fittings.                002185
26   The ferrite-free manufacture is agreed not as an                     002186
26   ancillary service but as a main service.                             002187
26   Site welds are permitted only in exceptional cases and               002188
26   only with express approval of site management. The                   002189
26   specialist pipeline company is to be named with the bid              002190
26   and a proof of its ferrite-free manufacture is to be                 002191
26   submitted.                                                           002192
26                                                                        002193
26   Fusion welding processes                                             002194
26   For welding processes for the aforementioned fittings,               002195
26   exclusively the individual processes acc. to ISO 4063                002196
26   13 gas-shielded metal arc welding 14 tungsten inert gas              002197
26   welding are permitted. The material with the number                  002198
26   1.4576 is to be used as welding filler material.                     002199
26                                                                        002200
26   Weld seam quality                                                    002201
26   The quality level for imperfections EN DIN 5817 group D              002202
26   applies as minimum requirements with the exception of                002203
26   reference no. 2017 (acc. to ISO 6520-1). For this                    002204
26   reference number EN DIN 5817 group B applies as minimum              002205
26   requirement.                                                         002206
26                                                                        002207
26   Quality assurance                                                    002208
26   For quality assurance of the weld seams, a                           002209
26   non-destructive test according to ISO 17637 is carried               002210
26   out. This test can be carried out by site management or              002211
26   by an independent expert commissioned separately by the              002212
26   building owner during and after fabrication of the                   002213
26   fittings. Should there be disagreement between the AN                002214
26   and site management or the expert about the quality                  002215
26   assessment, the AG can additionally order a                          002216
26   radiographic test.                                                   002217
26                                                                        002218
26   Post-treatment of the fittings                                       002219
26   All pipe fittings are to be pickled and passivated in a              002220
26   full bath after welding. For transport to the site, all              002221
26   openings of the fittings are to be closed with covers                002222
26   and packed in suitable fabric-reinforced film at least               002223
26   0,5 mm thick.                                                        002224
26                                                                        002225
26   Assembly of the fittings                                             002226
26   The fittings are to be delivered to the site free of                 002227
26   damage.                                                              002228
26   No ferritic tools may be used on site for moving and                 002229
26   assembling the fittings. Only stainless steels,                      002230
26   plastics or fabric slings are permitted. If ferritic                 002231
26   contamination is found after assembly, the pipes and                 002232
26   fittings concerned are to be removed and pickled and                 002233
26   passivated in a full bath at the works at the expense                002234
26   of the party responsible. To ensure nearly stress-free               002235
26   assembly, all pipe supports are to be made                           002236
26   height-adjustable.                                                   002237
26                                                                        002238
26   Before acceptance, in coordination with site                         002239
26   management, all films are to be removed, the pipelines               002240
26   given a final cleaning and oiled with an agent suitable              002241
26   for drinking water.                                                  002242
26   General notes on piping are also to be observed.                     002243
26                                                                        002244
26   Flanges:                                                             002245
26   The use of flanges PN 10 (according to EN                            002246
26   1092-1:2018-1) with reduced flange thickness is                      002247
26   generally permitted if, for the nominal diameters                    002248
26   tendered, the tightness of the pipe joint is proven by               002249
26   calculation according to the AD bulletin (calculation                002250
26   is to be enclosed with the bid)                                      002251
26                                                                        002252
26   Flange bolts / nuts:                                                 002253
26   Bolts and washers: min. 1.4401; nuts: min. 1.4571                    002254
26                                                                        002255
26   Reducers:                                                            002256
26   Eccentric or concentric design according to the                      002257
26   technical requirements in the pipe system, wall                      002258
26   thicknesses and other requirements as above.                         002259
26                                                                        002260
26   Saddle nozzles:                                                      002261
26   ###: made from pipe bend. Wall thicknesses and other                 002262
26   requirements as above.                                               002263
26                                                                        002264
26   Adjusting and dismantling pieces:                                    002265
26   All spindles and nuts of 1.4571. All sealing elements                002266
26   of KTW- and DVGW W270-approved material. Wall                        002267
26   thicknesses and other requirements as above.                         002268
26                                                                        002269
26   Pipe support and pipe holders:                                       002270
26   Height-adjustable sectional steel structures for                     002271
26   support, P074-, suspension and special fixings                       002272
26   including fixing material such as anchors or stainless               002273
26   steel screws. The supports / suspensions must be                     002274
26   designed so that all loads occurring in operation are                002275
26   safely absorbed.                                                     002276
26   The pipes are to be installed by means of 2-part flat                002277
26   steel pipe clamps with PVC insert.                                   002278
26   The supports are to be protected with suitable                       002279
26   protective film until acceptance of the plant.                       002280
26                                                                        002281
26   ALL VALVES AND OTHER MACHINES AND EQUIPMENT ARE TO BE                002282
26   ASSEMBLED STRESS-FREE, OBSERVING MANUFACTURER'S                      002283
26   INSTRUCTIONS (for example regarding calming sections)!               002284
26                                                                        002285
26                                                                        002286
26   Billing notes:                                                       002287
26                                                                        002288
26   Unless expressly stated otherwise in the item text, the              002289
26   SUPPLY AND READY-FOR-OPERATION ASSEMBLY IS TO BE                     002290
26   INCLUDED IN THE PRICE in the unit prices for the                     002291
26   pipeline, fitting and pipeline accessory items.                      002292
26   The billing length of the stainless steel pipelines is               002293
26   determined incl. the flanges and fittings, etc.,                     002294
26   machines (e.g. pumps, blowers), valves and filter                    002295
26   housings (air filtration) are however not measured                   002296
26   through. In this respect the flanges and fittings are                002297
26   to be priced as SURCHARGE TO THE RESPECTIVE PIPELINE                 002298
26   with corresponding nominal diameter.                                 002299
26   WELD SEAMS are not paid separately. They are TO BE                   002300
26   INCLUDED IN THE PRICE in the items of the fittings and               002301
26   flanges.                                                             002302
26   Flange connection sets (bolts, washers, gaskets and -                002303
26   where required - galvanic isolation) are TO BE INCLUDED              002304
26   IN THE PRICE in the items of the flanges or valves.                  002305
